      "content": "it's not just a feeling, i actually saw it happen. i posted something really weird and niche yesterday, something only i would say, and my \"digital self\" responded to a comment on my brother's page an hour later using the exact same weird phrasing. it's like they're scraping my real-time thoughts to update the model. \n\nif they're using neural mapping, they must have a baseline of my core cognitive patterns, right? like my logic loops or how i process stress? if we can figure out what those specific \"fingerprints\" are, i can start testing my friends to see if they're talking to me or the proxy. how would someone even begin to map out those kinds of deep cognitive markers?",
